Michael Clive Price writes:
>Colonies in space (the solar system) have two advantages, in the Final
>War with Earth: ... When Earth-gov' becomes too troublesome ...

Ryan Alan Porter, Nick Szabo and Phoenix make similar points.

While this may be comfort to space folk warring with earth folk, it
need be little comfort to anarchists seeking to avoid states.  This
thread started from Perry's comment:

>Maybe we should all just give up and move to space where the fools
>can't get to us. ... (Only half joking.)

This imagines the states are on earth, the anarchists in space.  But
there can be states in space too.  Unless most of space is anarchist,
the issue is the nature of war between powers in space.  If there are
locations where defense is cheaper than offense, then folks can be
relatively safe just be going to such places.  But if it's the other
way around, everyone is part of the big international game of
alliances and deterrence.

Some of us imagine fortress or stealth colonies, while others,
including me, see more lots of visible glass houses a stones throw
from everyone.  This is the issue that we need to address.  

