> Anyone have good/bad stories about Shaklee brand supplements?

Good quality, but weak (except for the C) and far far too expensive. 
Vites aren't like cars.  They are more or less parity products and when
they do differ, it is a tradeoff situation.  "Better" vitamin E is simply
vitamin E that is absorbed more and faster.  If you pay 30% more for
vitamin E that is absorbed only 5% faster/better than The Other Brand,
you are getting ripped off, since you could get the same result by taking
5% more vitamin E, which of course costs you 5% more, not 30% more.  

Thus I don't go for Shaklee stuff, the cost is not parallel with the
performance gain.

